<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anacopia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anakopia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anacopia was a hill fortress above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast at present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-athos">New Athos</a> in Abkhazia. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of the princes of Abasgia, who ruled as clients of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. Its successful defence against an Arab army around 737 raised the standing of its rulers, who later founded the Kingdom of Abkhazia. Ruins of its walls and towers survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anacopia.jpg" alt="Anacopia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alaexis · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Athos_Monastery.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
